From df67a980864695124d6f5b22df8e5c6dd471ea96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:00:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(contact): use api.whatsapp.com long form for
 click-to-chat links

The wa.me short domain is commonly blocked by ad blockers, privacy
extensions and DNS filters, which renders a blank page instead of
opening the chat. Switch every direct-contact link to the long form,
which carries the number as a ?phone= parameter and survives filters
that eat the short domain.

Converted 10 links across:
- web/site/home.html (contact block, footer emergency, chat widget)
- web/components/ChatBot.tsx
- web/app/links/page.tsx
- web/app/forgot-password/ForgotForm.tsx
- web/app/admin/AdminClient.tsx

In home.html the query separator is written &amp; so the href parses
correctly as raw HTML; the .tsx files keep a literal &.

The three wa.me/?text= share links in the service and store share
widgets are deliberately unchanged: they carry no phone number and are
meant to open a recipient picker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013E71HHNBrVB7D4V6VgonLA
